<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Autonomy stage: the cognition (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx)
  invokes it once and holds it for its lifetime, as mosfet.py's Cognition
  holds its Autonomy (decision D272), and hands it each turn first. It
  runs the trusted seeds the turn's stimulus triggers, then recalls the
  learned turn behaviors whose triggers name the stimulus, and runs them
  one at a time as candidates; the first that handles the turn answers it,
  and otherwise the cascade goes on to intuition.

    idle -bot.ability.autonomy.input-> working {
    percept { matching -> [seeding] -> inventory -> loading -> matched -> running {
                running_candidate -> dispatching -> using -> percept_handled
                running_candidate | dispatching -> recording_failure -> recorded_failure
                recorded_failure -> failed | advancing
                running_candidate -> advancing -> running_candidate (the next one) | percept_unhandled } }
       |  (each percept, in arrival order)
       v
    percept_handled | percept_unhandled -> next_percept -> percept (the next one)
                                                       -> answered | unhandled | done
    percept -> failed
    } -> answering -> idle
    working -bot.ability.processing.cancel-> idle

  (seeding runs only when the percept triggers a seed; inventory ends at
  once without memory.)

  Percepts: a turn that perceived several stimuli together (the body's
  bot.perceived) is matched percept by percept, in arrival order, each by its own name, and each
  matching behavior runs on the turn as that percept alone presents it
  (the percept's stimulus is the stimulus, view). A turn of one stimulus is
  its own one percept. The first behavior that handles a percept settles
  it; the turn is handled only when every percept was, with what the
  handling behaviors selected in the percepts' arrival order. Otherwise it
  is unhandled, and its answer carries those selections as acted
  {percepts, acts} (the handled percepts' positions and their
  selections). A selection that names no target (the trusted seed's) is not sent here: it reaches the body only when the
  cognition carries acted.acts into the turn's output.

  Input: each turn is one bot.ability.autonomy.input
  (schemas/bot.ability.autonomy.input.json) {turn, input (focus and
  focus_candidates), stimulus (the turn's stimulus envelope)}; one that
  arrives during a turn waits for its answer. The <param> memory is the
  address of the bot's memory (null means no learned inventory, and only
  the seeds run).

  Output: each turn ends with one bot.ability.autonomy.output
  (schemas/bot.ability.autonomy.output.json) to the cognition, the
  answers below. bot.ability.processing.cancel (the cognition left the
  turn) ends a turn in flight, with no answer, and cancels what it runs.

  Seeds (the seeded behaviors run before the learned inventory, with or
  without memory): SpeechHeard (abilities/behaviors/speech_heard/speech_heard.scx),
  triggered by
  bot.ability.listening.speech.output, runs as the child "seed" with the
  <param>s turn, input and stimulus (its input_adapter keeps the
  cognition's input unchanged). It answers as a candidate does: handled
  answers {turn, handled: true, selected, candidates, reason: "behavior"}
  with no usage persisted (a seed is not an inventory row); not handled,
  or silent within silence_ms, goes on to the inventory; an error.* for it
  fails autonomy ("Autonomy native seed 'SpeechHeard' failed: ...").
  candidates names it first. A seed's selections are trusted (they may name
  any event a recipient declares, not only the offered ones) and name no
  target: the turn's output carries them to the body, which sends itself
  the ones that name no target (its own bot.ability.communication.input).

  Matching: one memory transaction per percept selects the ACTIVE behaviors of lifetime 'turn' that have a
  trigger equal to the percept's event name, in inventory order (by name).
  No match answers {turn, handled: false, candidates: [], reason:
  "no-behaviors"}.

  Candidates (decision D93): running tries them one at a time, in
  inventory order (decision D273; they were a chain of candidates_runner
  children before). Each behavior's source is
  the path of its SCXML document (phase 5 plan, "Turn Behavior Contract"),
  which the builder wrote beside its schema file and script (decision
  D121), run in running_candidate as the child "candidate" by <invoke srcexpr>, with the <param>s
  turn and input
  (the stimulus's data, or {event: data} when it is not an object, plus
  focus and focus_candidates: <autonomy:behavior_input_payload>). It answers by
  its final state's <donedata> {turn, handled, selected}:
    * handled with selections: dispatching sends each to the session its
      target names (decision D113; a learned behavior names its targets,
      the session ids of its turn's selections). Sent, its used_count and
      last_used_at are persisted, then autonomy answers {turn, handled: true, selected, candidates,
      reason: "behavior"}. A send that fails, its failed_count and
      last_failed_at are persisted and autonomy fails with the failure's
      message, so the turn fails;
    * not handled (candidate.advance), or no answer within silence_ms
      (candidate.silent, decision D74): the next one runs;
    * an error.* for it (candidate.failed): its failed_count and
      last_failed_at are persisted, then the next one runs.
  When none handles the turn: {turn, handled: false, candidates, reason:
  "unhandled"}. candidates names the behaviors tried, in order.

  Memory: each transaction invokes the Memory ability (abilities/memory/memory.scx)
  with its statements. A transaction that fails or
  outlasts memory_timeout_ms is logged and the turn goes on: a failed
  load matches no inventory rows, and a failed usage or failure record
  takes the same effect as a persisted one
  (autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed).

  Timers: seeding and loading are entered once per percept, and
  running_candidate, using and recording_failure once per candidate, so each
  cancels its own timer on exit, and a later percept's or candidate's
  state never takes an earlier one's.

  Contracts: the Memory ability's events reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema. A candidate is builder output, loaded from its path with
  the schema file and script beside it.

  Bindings: the autonomy namespace package (the Memory ability binds the
  sql service).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:autonomy="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/autonomy"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="autonomy" initial="idle">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="input" expr="null"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D266). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="silence_ms" expr="1000"/>
    <data id="memory_timeout_ms" expr="10000"/>
    <data id="rows" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="tried" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="behavior_input" expr="null"/>
    <data id="answer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The turn's percepts (stimulus envelopes in arrival order), the
         position of the one being matched and its stimulus (view), the
         positions a behavior handled, and what the handling behaviors
         selected, in arrival order. -->
    <data id="percepts" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="position" expr="0"/>
    <data id="view" expr="null"/>
    <data id="handled" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="selected" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The candidates left to try ([{name, source}], the first running),
         the handled candidate's selection being sent (the <foreach> item),
         and why its dispatch failed (null when sent). -->
    <data id="candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
    <data id="rejection" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The turn's answer, sent to the cognition. -->
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <data id="used_sql">UPDATE bot_behavior SET used_count = CAST(CAST(used_count AS INTEGER) + 1 AS TEXT), last_used_at = replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z' WHERE name = ?</data>
    <data id="failed_sql">UPDATE bot_behavior SET failed_count = CAST(CAST(failed_count AS INTEGER) + 1 AS TEXT), last_failed_at = replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z' WHERE name = ?</data>
    <data id="select_sql">SELECT b.name, b.source FROM bot_behavior AS b JOIN bot_behavior_trigger AS t ON t.behavior_name = b.name WHERE b.status = 'ACTIVE' AND b.lifetime = 'turn' AND t."trigger" = ? ORDER BY b.name</data>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="autonomy.js"/>

  <!-- Between turns: each bot.ability.autonomy.input is one turn, with
       nothing of the turn before. -->
  <state id="idle">
    <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.autonomy.input.json"
                target="percept">
      <assign location="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      <assign location="input" expr="_event.data.input"/>
      <assign location="stimulus" expr="_event.data.stimulus"/>
      <assign location="rows" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="tried" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behavior_input" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="answer" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="position" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="handled" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="null"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- One turn; leaving it (the cognition left the turn) cancels what it
       runs. -->
  <state id="working" initial="percept">
    <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.autonomy.input.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The cognition left the turn (cancelled or timed out). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.cancel.json"
                target="idle"/>

    <!-- One percept: the seeds it triggers, then the learned inventory. -->
    <state id="percept" initial="matching">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="percepts" expr="perceptsOf(stimulus)"/>
        <assign location="view" expr="currentPercept()"/>
        <assign location="rows" expr="[]"/>
      </onentry>

      <!-- The seeds the percept triggers run first. -->
      <state id="matching">
        <transition cond="triggersSpeechHeard()" target="seeding"/>
        <transition target="inventory"/>
      </state>

      <!-- The SpeechHeard seed. -->
      <state id="seeding">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="tried" expr="triedWithSeed()"/>
          <log label="autonomy.candidate" expr="'SpeechHeard'"/>
          <send id="seed-silence" event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.silent" delayexpr="silenceDelay()"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="seed-silence"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="seed" type="scxml" src="../behaviors/speech_heard/speech_heard.scx">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="input" expr="input"/>
          <param name="stimulus" expr="view"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.seed" cond="isBehaviorHandled(_event)" target="percept_handled">
          <assign location="answer" expr="_event.data.selected"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.seed" target="inventory">
          <log label="autonomy.candidate.advance" expr="seedAdvanceLog(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.silent" target="inventory">
          <log label="autonomy.candidate.silent" expr="seedSilentLog()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="failed">
          <assign location="answer" expr="seedFailedReason(_event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Then the learned inventory, when there is memory. -->
      <state id="inventory">
        <onentry>
          <if cond="hasNoMemory()">
            <log label="autonomy" expr="noMemoryLog()"/>
          </if>
        </onentry>
        <transition cond="hasNoMemory()" target="percept_unhandled"/>
        <transition target="loading"/>
      </state>

      <!-- The inventory: the ACTIVE turn behaviors the percept triggers. -->
      <state id="loading">
        <onentry>
          <send id="load-timeout" event="bot.ability.autonomy.behaviors.load.failed" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="load-timeout"/>
        </onexit>
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.load">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.load"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="behaviorSelectStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('load')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="matched">
          <assign location="rows" expr="behaviorsFromMemoryOutput(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- A failed load is a warning, and the turn goes on with no inventory rows. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('load')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="matched">
          <log label="autonomy.behaviors.load.failed" expr="loadFailedReason(_event.data.message)"/>
          <assign location="rows" expr="[]"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="matched">
          <log label="autonomy.behaviors.load.failed" expr="loadFailedReason(_event.name)"/>
          <assign location="rows" expr="[]"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.behaviors.load.failed" target="matched">
          <log label="autonomy.behaviors.load.failed" expr="loadTimedOutReason()"/>
          <assign location="rows" expr="[]"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <state id="matched">
        <onentry>
          <log label="autonomy" expr="matchedLog()"/>
        </onentry>
        <transition cond="hasNoMatch()" target="percept_unhandled"/>
        <transition target="running"/>
      </state>

      <!-- The candidates, one at a time (decision D93). -->
      <state id="running" initial="running_candidate">
        <onentry>
          <autonomy:behavior_input_payload location="behavior_input" stimulus="view"
              focus="input.focus" focus_candidates="input.focus_candidates"/>
          <assign location="candidates" expr="candidateRows()"/>
        </onentry>

        <!-- The first candidate left. -->
        <state id="running_candidate">
          <onentry>
            <assign location="tried" expr="triedWithCandidate()"/>
            <assign location="rejection" expr="null"/>
            <log label="autonomy.candidate" expr="candidateName()"/>
            <send id="candidate-silence" event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.silent" delayexpr="silenceDelay()"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="candidate-silence"/>
          </onexit>
          <invoke id="candidate" type="scxml" srcexpr="candidateSource()">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
            <param name="input" expr="behavior_input"/>
          </invoke>
          <transition event="done.invoke.candidate" cond="isBehaviorHandled(_event)" target="dispatching">
            <assign location="answer" expr="_event.data.selected"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="done.invoke.candidate" target="advancing">
            <log label="autonomy.candidate.advance" expr="candidateAdvanceLog(_event)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.silent" target="advancing">
            <log label="autonomy.candidate.silent" expr="candidateSilentLog()"/>
          </transition>
          <!-- A source that does not load or compile fails the invocation
               with no invokeid (SCXML 3.12.2). -->
          <transition event="error.*" target="recording_failure">
            <log label="autonomy.candidate.failed" expr="candidateFailedLog(_event)"/>
          </transition>
        </state>

        <!-- The handled candidate's selections are sent before its use is
             persisted. -->
        <state id="dispatching">
          <onentry>
            <foreach array="answer" item="s">
              <send eventexpr="s.event" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + s.target">
                <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
              </send>
            </foreach>
          </onentry>
          <!-- Its own block, so it runs after a send that failed above and
               the failure (raised first) preempts it. -->
          <onentry>
            <raise event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.dispatch.succeeded"/>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.candidate.dispatch.succeeded" target="using"/>
          <transition event="error.*" target="recording_failure">
            <assign location="rejection" expr="dispatchFailure(_event)"/>
            <log label="autonomy.candidate.failed" expr="candidateRejectedLog()"/>
          </transition>
        </state>

        <!-- The handled candidate's use is persisted, then it handles the
             percept. -->
        <state id="using">
          <onentry>
            <send id="usage-timeout" event="bot.ability.autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.usage">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.usage"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="usedPersistenceStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="usage-timeout"/>
          </onexit>
          <!-- The update's results: nothing to keep. -->
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('usage')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="percept_handled"/>
          <!-- A failed persistence takes the same effect as one persisted. -->
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('usage')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="percept_handled">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageFailedReason(_event.data.message)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="error.*" target="percept_handled">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageFailedReason(_event.name)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" target="percept_handled">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageTimedOutReason()"/>
          </transition>
        </state>

        <!-- A failed candidate's failure is persisted, then the rest run; a
             rejected one's, then autonomy fails with the rejection. -->
        <state id="recording_failure">
          <onentry>
            <send id="failure-timeout" event="bot.ability.autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.failure">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.failure"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="failedPersistenceStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="failure-timeout"/>
          </onexit>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('failure')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="recorded_failure"/>
          <!-- A failed persistence takes the same effect as one persisted. -->
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('failure')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="recorded_failure">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageFailedReason(_event.data.message)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="error.*" target="recorded_failure">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageFailedReason(_event.name)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" target="recorded_failure">
            <log label="autonomy.behavior_usage.persistence_failed" expr="usageTimedOutReason()"/>
          </transition>
        </state>

        <state id="recorded_failure">
          <transition cond="isRejected()" target="failed">
            <assign location="answer" expr="rejection"/>
          </transition>
          <transition target="advancing"/>
        </state>

        <!-- The next candidate, or the percept is unhandled. -->
        <state id="advancing">
          <transition cond="hasRest()" target="running_candidate">
            <assign location="candidates" expr="restCandidates()"/>
          </transition>
          <transition target="percept_unhandled"/>
        </state>
      </state>
    </state>

    <!-- A behavior handled the percept: it is settled. -->
    <state id="percept_handled">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="handled" expr="handledWithPercept()"/>
        <assign location="selected" expr="selectedWithAnswer()"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="next_percept"/>
    </state>
    <state id="percept_unhandled">
      <transition target="next_percept"/>
    </state>

    <!-- The next percept, or the turn's answer: handled only when every
         percept was. -->
    <state id="next_percept">
      <transition cond="hasNextPercept()" target="percept">
        <assign location="position" expr="nextPosition()"/>
      </transition>
      <transition cond="everyPerceptHandled()" target="answered"/>
      <transition cond="hasNoCandidates()" target="done"/>
      <transition target="unhandled"/>
    </state>

    <state id="done">
      <onentry><assign location="result" expr="noBehaviorsOutput()"/></onentry>
      <transition target="answering"/>
    </state>

    <state id="unhandled">
      <onentry><assign location="result" expr="unhandledOutput()"/></onentry>
      <transition target="answering"/>
    </state>

    <state id="answered">
      <onentry><assign location="result" expr="answeredOutput()"/></onentry>
      <transition target="answering"/>
    </state>

    <state id="failed">
      <onentry><assign location="result" expr="failedOutput()"/></onentry>
      <transition target="answering"/>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- The turn's answer to the cognition, then the next turn. -->
  <state id="answering">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.autonomy.output" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="result"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <transition target="idle"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
